From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:36:34 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0104): first-run provisioning (server or LAN only,
 permanent password)

On first launch with no ID server and no "Direct LAN only" choice, or with no
permanent password, the desktop home page shows a setup dialog:
- ID server host + public key (validated: host[:port], 44-char base64
  Ed25519 key), or paste an exported server config, or Direct LAN only
  (option remotesmith-lan-only=Y);
- a permanent password of at least 12 characters, with a generator
  (20 chars from the OS CSPRNG, no look-alike characters).
Values go through the same option/password calls as Settings, so they are
stored in upstream's config (password hashed/encrypted as upstream does).
Nothing is prefilled.

Headless: --option custom-rendezvous-server/key/remotesmith-lan-only and
--password now apply the same validation. The Settings password dialog
minimum goes from 8 to 12. Logic and tests live in src/remotesmith.rs; four
small FFI functions expose it to Flutter.

Plan: FLOW-2, DEC-10, DEF-2, AC-40, AC-10.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
